l = await listSources();        // full select + zod-parse of every row\n  return {\n    crm: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"salesforce\" || s.kind === \"hubspot\").length,\n    warehouse: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"databricks\" || s.kind === \"snowflake\").length,\n    synthetic: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"synthetic\").length,\n  };\n}\n```\n\nHarmless at today's scale (a handful of sources), but push the counts into SQL so it stays cheap as the table grows:\n\n```ts\nimport { sql } from \"drizzle-orm\";\n\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  const [row] = await getDb()\n    .select({\n      crm: sql<number>`count(*) filter (where kind in ('salesforce','hubspot'))`,\n      warehouse: sql<number>`count(*) filter (where kind in ('databricks','snowflake'))`,\n      synthetic: sql<number>`count(*) filter (where kind = 'synthetic')`,\n    })\n    .from(sources);\n  return row;\n}\n```\n\n## Caching opportunities — one worth doing now\n\n`listSources()` isn't currently called twice in the same request, so there's no live bug. But `countSourcesBySide()` internally calls it, and if a future page ever needs both the list *and* the count in one render (e.g., a shared layout), that's two DB round-trips for identical data. Wrap it in React's `cache()` so calls within one request dedupe automatically — cheap insurance, no downside:\n\n```ts\nimport { cache } from \"react\";\n\nexport const listSources = cache(async (): Promise<Source[]> => {\n  await connection();\n  const rows = await getDb().select().from(sources).orderBy(sources.createdAt);\n  return rows.map((row) => sourceSchema.parse(row));\n});\n```\n\nNote `connection()` (`lib/server/sources.ts:17`) is already correctly opting this out of static prerendering since the source list is request-time state — don't touch that part.\n\n## Bottom line\n\nNothing urgent. The one thing worth doing now, while it's a one-line diff, is #1 (SQL-side counts) — it's the single place a full-table-then-filter pattern is baked into the code path rather than something that grew organically. `cache()` on `listSources` is optional insurance for later, not a fix for a current bug.\n",
